+# Agent Note: Checked Session Model Migration
+
+Status: implemented
+
+English | [中文](2026-09-10-checked-session-model-migration.zh.md)
+
+## Problem
+
+A model selection can change more than the next request's route. A destination may have a smaller context window than the retained conversation requires, and an OpenAI Responses-compatible reasoning gateway may require plaintext reasoning items beside historical tool calls. Applying the selection before checking those facts can leave an established Session unable to continue, while starting a replacement Session discards the work the user intended to retain.
+
+The check must observe one stable Session state. A capacity result computed while a turn or queued input changes the retained surface is stale before it can be committed. It also cannot use the source route's token accounting or an adapter-supplied output default as if either were a user choice.
+
+## Decision
+
+`session.selectModel` accepts the opt-in `migration: "checked"` mode. The controller admits it only while the Agent is idle and its inbox is empty, then owns the Agent's maintenance phase until the destination check either rejects or appends `model/selection`. Input arriving during that phase remains queued; a changed log revision, pending input, or cancellation rejects the operation before the selection event. The caller can retry after the Agent settles.
+
+The controller resolves a prepared destination call without dispatching it. It reconstructs the latest request proposal, removes adapter-defaulted `maxTokens` and reasoning effort, applies the requested route and optional effort, and lets the destination adapter supply its defaults. An explicit output allowance remains explicit. The token meter prices the retained surface plus the latest system prompt and tool schemas under the destination route. The check accepts `inputTokens + maxTokens === contextWindow` and rejects a larger sum, an unknown context window, or an unknown output allowance. It never compacts, truncates, or summarizes history.
+
+A successful checked migration appends the ordinary durable `model/selection` event and changes only that Session. It does not save the deployment default. Projection replay restores the pending selection after reopening, and the next matching request header consumes it through the existing model-selection mechanism. An unsuccessful check appends nothing and performs no generation request, so the source route remains selected and usable.
+
+For a pi-ai route that sets `responsesReasoningText: true`, every model must use `openai-responses`. When historical assistant content came from another API, provider, or model and contains tool calls, the adapter emits each available plaintext reasoning block as an ordered Responses `reasoning` item. It removes source response ids, item ids, signatures, and other opaque replay state, while retaining the call id needed to pair each function call with its result. Exact same-route replay keeps the validated native metadata. Disabled routes keep the existing serialization behavior. Durable messages are never rewritten.
+
+## Existing decisions and supersession
+
+This decision narrows [the default model follows the picker](../feature/2026-08-07-default-model-follows-the-picker.md): ordinary selections still update the deployment default, while checked migrations are deliberately Session-local. It extends [provider-routed LLM adapters](2026-07-14-provider-routed-llm-adapters.md) and [max-token replay-state alignment](../bug-fix/2026-08-15-max-token-replay-state-alignment.md) with an explicit destination-owned conversion that discards source-native metadata. Their replay ownership and degradation rules remain authoritative.
+
+The [replay token meter service](2026-07-15-replay-token-meter-service.md) and [route-priced image request pressure](../feature/2026-08-24-route-priced-image-request-pressure.md) remain active without supersession: checked migration is another consumer of their existing candidate-header repricing behavior. No related active note is fully superseded or eligible for archival.
+
+## Verification
+
+A real-loop test performs a source-provider tool turn, checks a destination, reconstructs the Session from its saved events, continues on the destination, executes another tool call, and continues after its result. Focused cases cover active and queued Sessions, input arriving during asynchronous destination resolution, missing capacity facts, overflow, equality at the capacity limit, source-route usability after rejection, destination default replacement, explicit output allowance preservation, Session locality, and the absence of provider generation during checks. pi-ai conversion and raw-wire tests cover ordered reasoning/text/parallel-call output, result pairing, foreign metadata removal, same-route fidelity, disabled behavior, and profile validation.
+
+## Alternatives considered
+
+**Switch first and rely on the next request's overflow handling.** Rejected because selection succeeds even when the Session cannot continue, and recovery may compact or fail only after mutating durable state.
+
+**Estimate from the previous request unchanged.** Rejected because context capacity, image pricing, reasoning defaults, and output allowance belong to the destination route. An adapter default is not an explicit caller choice.
+
+**Serialize every historical reasoning block as Responses reasoning.** Rejected because reasoning items matter for tool-call continuity and labeling ordinary reasoning-only messages as destination-native changes established serialization without a compatibility need.
+
+**Reuse source replay metadata on the destination.** Rejected because response ids, item ids, signatures, and encrypted reasoning are scoped to the source API route and can be invalid or unsafe on another route.
+
+## Consequences
+
+Checked selection performs destination capability resolution and O(surface) token estimation before it can commit. It proves only that the retained work fits at that moment; later prompts can exceed capacity, and external provider availability can still change. Deployments must opt compatible Responses routes into plaintext reasoning replay, and they cannot enable that option on mixed or non-Responses routes.
