+## Checked model migration
+
+Clients opt into a retained-work check with `session.selectModel({ sessionId, provider, model, migration: "checked" })`. The Session must be idle with no pending input. The Host resolves the destination's context window and effective output allowance, reprices the retained conversation plus the latest system prompt and tool schemas through `ctx.tokenMeter`, and accepts the selection only when the sum fits. An explicit prior `maxTokens` remains in force; an adapter-defaulted value is replaced by the destination default. Missing capacity information and concurrent Session changes are rejections, and no check dispatches a provider generation.
+
+A successful checked migration appends the ordinary `model/selection` event, so reopening the Session preserves the route. It does not change the deployment default or any other Session. A rejected migration appends nothing and leaves the current route usable. The check is a statement about retained work at selection time, not a reservation for later prompts or provider availability. See [the checked-migration decision](../../.agents/notes/implemented/architecture/2026-09-10-checked-session-model-migration.md).
+
 ## Remote catalog and workspace opening
 
 `ModelCatalog` is the Host-generation model directory returned by `session/modelCatalog`: it carries the deployment default, routable provider ids, successful provider groups, and isolated provider failures. It is not derived from one Session and remains separate from Session projections.
